# Keep __cfi_check in the dynamic symbol table of every library this tree
# builds, whatever its own version script says.
#
# tools/configure copies this beside each layer's response files and
# tools/lib/toolchain.py names it in LDFLAGS, so it is appended to every link
# that keeps cross-DSO CFI -- not something a recipe opts into.
#
# WHY A SECOND VERSION SCRIPT
#
# Cross-DSO CFI dispatches into a shared object through that object's own
# __cfi_check, and the runtime finds it BY NAME in the object's dynamic symbol
# table: compiler-rt/lib/cfi/cfi.cpp:216 walks DT_SYMTAB looking for the
# string. When it is not there, :299 marks the module's whole address range
# kUncheckedShadow and every indirect call into that library passes without a
# check. No error, no warning, no missing symbol at link time -- the library
# just stops being covered.
#
# Upstream version scripts end `local: *;` as a matter of course, and
# __cfi_check is not part of anybody's public API, so it is exactly what
# `local: *;` is for. Measured on clang 19.1.1 -- which was the Containerfile's
# LLVM until this tree's base became Arch -- after an earlier round was made
# only on a developer box's 18.1.3, and repeated on 18.1.3, with mold and with
# lld in both cases. The Arch base installs whatever pacman currently ships and
# reported clang 22.1.8 / LLVM 22.1.8 / mold 2.42.1 on the run that switched
# it, so the container's compiler is now three majors past the newest of those
# measurements and nobody has repeated them there. Two rounds of "still
# reproduces" is a trend, not a proof that 22 behaves the same. What was
# measured: a
# library built with cross-DSO CFI and linked with a `global: api_*; local: *;`
# script exports no __cfi_check at all. That is most of the version scripts in
# this tree -- tpm2-tss ships one per library, and cryptsetup, linux-pam,
# p11-kit, libpwquality, libfido2, libunistring, libtasn1, gnutls and curl all
# have one.
#
# A second --version-script naming the symbol promotes it back. Measured, both
# orders, mold and lld: the package's own versioning is untouched
# (`api_one@@THEIR_VERSION` stays exactly that) and __cfi_check comes back
# unversioned. Promotion can work at all only because __cfi_check is STV_DEFAULT
# even under -fvisibility=hidden. A version script cannot promote a symbol the
# compiler already made hidden, which is why this file does nothing for the
# separate problem the `drops: [visibility]` exceptions in
# manifest/toolchain.yaml exist for -- the two look alike and are not related.
#
# The alternatives do not work, and were tried rather than reasoned about:
# -Wl,--export-dynamic-symbol=__cfi_check and -Wl,--dynamic-list= both leave
# the symbol local under `local: *;`, on mold and on lld alike.
#
# WHY THE NAME IS SPELLED AS A GLOB
#
# `__cfi_chec[k]` matches exactly __cfi_check and nothing else, but it is a
# PATTERN, and a pattern that matches nothing is silent. Spelled as a plain
# name it is an exact assignment, and a link with no __cfi_check in it -- a
# package carrying `drops: [cfi]`, anything in losos-00-toolchain, every
# configure probe that links a five-line test program -- gets
#
#     mold: warning: cannot assign version `global` to symbol `__cfi_check`:
#     symbol not found
#
# on mold, and on lld the same thing as a hard error. Since this file is on
# every link in the tree, that is the difference between a no-op and a build
# that cannot run a configure test. Measured both ways.
#
# There is no `local:` here on purpose. A version script that restricts nothing
# is a no-op for a library that has no script of its own: measured, a library
# linked with this file alone still exports everything it did before.
#
# Tombstone: ld.bfd cannot do this at all -- "anonymous version tag cannot be
# combined with other version tags" -- so a tree that went back to bfd would
# need every package's own script patched instead. mold is what
# manifest/toolchain.yaml selects and lld is the fallback; both are fine.
{
  global: __cfi_chec[k];
};
